.TH ASSETS_PATH 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
assets_path \- Build the absolute path of a file under assets/ into buf (n bytes) and return buf
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqassets.h\(dq
.BI "const char  * assets_path(const char *relative_path, char *buf, size_t n);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Build the absolute path of a file under assets/ into buf (n bytes) and return buf. assets/ is located next to the executable, where CMake copies the project's assets/ folder after each build. Use it to open your own data files (level text, dialogue scripts, CSV tables) with fopen: char p[1024]; FILE *f = fopen(assets_path("levels/1.txt", p, sizeof p), "rb");.
.SH RETURN VALUE
buf, for use directly inside a call.
.SH MODULE
assets (src/engine/assets/assets.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR assets_texture (3),
.BR tilemap_load_csv (3),
.BR gge\-assets (7),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
